---
title: "Protein Oat Bars"
summary: "Delicious and simple protein bar recipe for the whole family"
publishedDate: 2025-09-12
heroImage: /images/recipes/protein-oat-bars.webp
pillar: blood-sugar
cta: book-consult
prepMinutes: 15
cookMinutes: 25
servings: "14 squares"
ingredients:
  - "2.5 cups rolled oats (gluten free, organic recommended)"
  - "1/2 cup shredded coconut"
  - "1/2 cup sunflower seeds (toasted is yummy)"
  - "1/2 cup currants"
  - "1/2 cup mini chocolate chips (optional, fun for kids)"
  - "1/2 cup collagen protein powder (or favorite protein powder)"
  - "1 tsp cinnamon"
  - "1/2 tsp sea salt"
  - "2 eggs"
  - "1 tsp vanilla extract"
  - "1/3 cup nut butter (or sunbutter for nut-free)"
  - "1/3 cup honey or maple syrup (I like half of each)"
steps:
  - "Preheat oven to 350 degrees F."
  - "Line an 8x8 or 9x9 baking dish with parchment."
  - "Combine all the dry ingredients in a bowl, including currants, chocolate chips and protein powder - mix well."
  - "In a separate bowl, whisk together the eggs, vanilla, nut butter and honey/maple syrup."
  - "Pour the wet ingredients over the dry ingredients and stir well with a spatula to evenly combine."
  - "Press mixture into the baking dish, and continue to press down firmly with palm to flatten and pack down the mixture."
  - "Bake for 20-25 minutes, until just lightly browned on edges, remove from oven and allow to cool."
  - "Lift up on parchment to remove from dish, cut into squares once fully cooled."
  - "Store in an airtight container in fridge for 1 week or in freezer for up to 3 months."
legacyUrl: /treats/protein-oat-bars
---

The world of protein bars is a an overwhelming place. Too much sugar, not enough protein, don’t taste good, too expensive…. but we need to have those on-the-go options to help us through our day, right?

Here is a recipe that I promise is not too complicated to make, with a proper balance of flavor and protein with just a hint of sweet. I made these for my daughter to take to school (nut-free option!) but now I’m finding they’re a great mid-afternoon snack for myself.
